MID_SE_Dit_Set_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_001: Some time ago I told you I'd allow you to keep that\nsword. Tell me. Have you learned anything since?
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_002: As I have engaged in battle, the strongest emotions\nof my opponents have reached me.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_003: Pride. Fealty. Atonement. Resolve. Love. These\nthings, and still more.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_004: Good. Soon enough, you'll be able to understand the\nemotions of others through conversation too.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_005: Let us begin, then. I have a question for you.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_006: Why is it that you remain in this land and throw\nyourself into battle?
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_007: Obvious, isn't it? It's become impossible to overlook\nthe strangeness here in Dagda.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_008: Gods and humans have lost their way. The natural\norder has deteriorated. It's verging on mayhem.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_009: You must sense this.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_010: Yes. My days are filled with pleasurable chaos.\nI welcome it...
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_011: This situation is unnatural. Laws are laws. Things\nmust be put right again.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_012: Why? Is there some meaning in doing this?
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_013: Perhaps not to you. But there is value in order.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_014: In war, there are winners and losers, yes. But war\nalso victimizes the innocent masses.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_015: I once thrust myself headlong into the heat of battle,\nno matter the threat.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_016: I was driven by the desire not to lose my comrades,\nmy family...or anything, really.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_017: But every day...blood flowed. So much blood. And\neven my beloved wife was lost.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_018: Hm...
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_019: For my daughter, who had lost her mother, I swore\nthat I would never let such a war unfold again.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_020: Your place is in Fódlan. The peace you protect\nis there.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_021: It's not so simple, though. The chaos here bleeds\ninto the wide world, Fódlan included.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_022: I owe a strong debt to that land. It falls to me to\nsubdue the disturbance here.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_023: The peace, the happiness of the entire world is at\nstake. I must do what I can.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_024: And so you play your part, fighting for the sake of\nthe world... Incomprehensible.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_025: Your words fall like ash before me. They express\nnothing I can fathom.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_C_026: Is that so? I pray that one day you may\nunderstand them.
MID_SE_Dit_Set_B: 
